\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 STEP 2: The "Would They Share It?" Test\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 "Would a busy CC faculty member share this with a colleague?"\strokec2 \
If the answer is "probably not," reject it \'97 even if it passed Step 1. This is the broad appeal test. A story about one school getting a grant fails this. A story about 43% of all graduates being underemployed passes this. The difference is: does the reader see THEMSELVES in it, or does it feel like someone else's news?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 STEP 3: The "That's Interesting" Framework (which facts to highlight)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 From the Davis research \'97 a fact is interesting when it challenges an assumption the audience holds. Look for:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 TENSION:
\f2\b0  Two facts that seem contradictory (95% use AI but 82% fear it will cost them jobs)\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 REVERSAL:
\f2\b0  A fact that defies what educators assume\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 SCALE:
\f2\b0  A number bigger or smaller than expected (94,000 survey responses)\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 CONNECTION:
\f2\b0  Two unrelated things that are linked\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 CHANGE:
\f2\b0  Something stable that's shifting, or something chaotic that's stabilizing\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

